# Stmt::Echo used to compile its value but never free the register(s)
# it used, unlike the otherwise-identical Stmt::Expression right next
# to it in the compiler. Every echo permanently leaked at least one
# register, so a few hundred sequential echoes (plain or method-call)
# in the same scope blew past the 255-register ceiling: a graceful
# SyntaxError for a bare value, but an unchecked u8 add overflow (a
# hard panic) for a method-invoke echo. This file exercises enough of
# both to catch a regression.
